{"type": "say", "text": "Good morning everyone. We're here for the readiness review on the real-time collaboration service ahead of Monday's 09:00 UTC production launch. As I understand it, the service passed its staging tests — functional, failover, and basic load — and the draft launch plan currently enables the feature for 10% of accounts initially, permits up to 10,000 concurrent connections, uses the client library's default 5-second retry interval, stores collaboration data in the primary production region, and retains session transcripts for 90 days. Before I finalize and record the binding policy, I want to give backend engineering, reliability, privacy, and customer success each a chance to do their final check-in. Who would like to start?"}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF4", "text": "I need to flag a customer-success concern before we finalize. I reconciled the customer-success rollout spreadsheet an hour ago and confirmed that six accounts — acct-204, acct-219, acct-233, acct-241, acct-278, and acct-301 — have administrator opt-out commitments until their enablement sessions are complete. Those six accounts must be excluded from Monday's rollout. I have not updated the launch checklist yet, so we need to make sure these exclusions are reflected in the binding policy before Maya records it."}
```

